Z||000000||TwisT||07-16-2001||05:33 PM||||Hello once again!<P>Yes it's me...  Brett,  "Mr. Carribean."<P>I've been busy working and preparing for my Carribean experience,  and haven't been in Pennock's in a while.  I'm heading there sometime after Nov. 1st.<P>So what's been up?  <P>I see one or two new South Dakota members in the Forum since I was last here...  cool!  For those who don't know about me or remember me,  I have an '88 GT and live in Yankton SD.  I've been a long time Pennock member who now is heading to the island of St. Martin to live with my girlfriend...<P>I'm posting this now is because I need some help.  I've come to the critical point with my Fiero,  where it needs to be painted and reassembled.  I have the parts needed to finish it (it's currently stripped of all body panels except for the roof).  The problem is,  I have no body experience and no facilities to finish it,  let alone the time to do it in.<P>What I'm looking for is an experienced Fiero enthusiast who would be willing to help.  I can deliver the Fiero,  and will also pick it up.  My main concern is having a decent job done (doesn't have to be show quality),  as I will sell the car after it's completed.<P>Here's the kicker.  For that individual who takes upon the task of painting/ reassembling my Fiero,   I will buy them a plane ticket to St. Martin AND provide a place to stay,  food to eat,  beer to drink (he he he!),  and etc...  it's as simple as that!  The date and length of the trip can be discussed,  as well as all the other little details.  I'll be happy to work with that individual accordingly,  so that they have the time of their life!<P>This is no joke people!  =)  <P>GTBastard,  I give you first dibbs.  If you can't do it,  I will then pass on the torch on a first come first serve basis.  <P>Responses can be posted here,  or feel free to email me at tribaldust@dtgnet.com<P>I'll keep everyone updated on who the lucky one will be!<P>One last thought:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/palms.JPG"> <P><BR>The Carribean Fool,<P>Brett Aker<BR> <P>  ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||07-16-2001||08:32 PM||||Woah.<BR>I'm willing to LEARN bodywork for that!<P>Yeah, I remember you.  Actually I remember that pic of your beautiful g/f!  Glad you haven't forgotten us landlubbers.  Been a lot happening here since you left, but I'll just let you make your own opinions.<P>Good luck with the car!<P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator<p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 07-16-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||TwisT||07-16-2001||08:59 PM||||Thanks Chuck...  =)<P>The way I figure it...  why pay a body shop mucho dollars to have it done when I can give someone an opportunity of a life time?  Makes sense to me!<P>I am going to miss the fun I've had with Fieros and the Fiero community.  Fiero owner's have always been,  to me,  a very unique and very distinguished group of people;  not your run-of-the-mill auto enthusiasts.  I hope that the recent child-like infringement in this Forum's ranks won't completely ruin it.  There's a lot of cool people in here,  and a lot of information you just won't get anywhere else.<P>Yes,  she is beautiful!...<P>Brett   ||||reg||1
